.\" libsys.7 - System Call Wrapper Library
.TH LIBSYS 7 "January 2026" "Substrate" "Substrate Programmer's Manual"
.SH NAME
libsys \- C language interface to Substrate system calls
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall.h>
.PP
.BI "long syscall(long " number ", ...);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B libsys
is a static library providing the C language interface to the Substrate
kernel's system call interface. It serves as the lowest-level userspace
mechanism for invoking kernel services.
.PP
The library provides:
.IP \(bu 3
.BR syscall ()
\- A variadic function for invoking any system call by number.
.IP \(bu 3
Typed wrapper functions for commonly used system calls.
.IP \(bu 3
System call number definitions (SYS_* constants).
.SS System Call Mechanism
On i386, system calls are invoked via software interrupt 0x80.
Arguments are passed in registers:
.IP \(bu 3
System call number: EAX
.IP \(bu 3
Argument 1: EBX
.IP \(bu 3
Argument 2: ECX
.IP \(bu 3
Argument 3: EDX
.IP \(bu 3
Argument 4: ESI
.IP \(bu 3
Argument 5: EDI
.IP \(bu 3
Argument 6: EBP
.PP
Return value is placed in EAX. Negative values indicate errors (negated errno).
.SS Available Wrapper Functions
.TP
.BR vm86 (2)
Enter Virtual 8086 mode for legacy BIOS calls.
.SS Memory Management System Calls
The following syscalls are available for memory management:
.TP
.BI "void *mmap(void *" addr ", size_t " len ", int " prot ", int " flags ", int " fd ", off_t " offset ");"
Map files or anonymous memory into address space.
.TP
.BI "int munmap(void *" addr ", size_t " len ");"
Unmap a memory region.
.TP
.BI "int mprotect(void *" addr ", size_t " len ", int " prot ");"
Change memory protection flags.
.TP
.BI "void *brk(void *" addr ");"
Change the program break (data segment end).
.SH USAGE
Link with
.B \-lsys
and include the appropriate headers:
.PP
.nf
#include <sys/syscall.h>

int main(void) {
    /* Direct syscall invocation */
    long pid = syscall(SYS_getpid);
    
    /* Using typed wrapper */
    int ret = vm86(&info);
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I lib/sys/libsys.a
Static library archive.
.TP
.I lib/sys/include/sys/syscall.h
System call numbers and prototypes.
.SH NOTES
.B libsys
is separate from
.BR libc (7)
to allow minimal programs to invoke system calls without linking the
full C library. Programs using standard I/O or other libc features
should link with
.B \-lc
instead or in addition.
.PP
The calling convention matches the Linux i386 syscall ABI for
compatibility with the Linux personality emulation layer.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR syscall (2),
.BR vm86 (2),
.BR mmap (2),
.BR munmap (2),
.BR mprotect (2),
.BR brk (2),
.BR libc (7),
.BR substrate (7)
.SH HISTORY
.B libsys
first appeared in Substrate 0.1.
